  <!-- ===== [Nation] Harp God — the one nobody was given ===== -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="BaseWeapon">
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_HarpGod</defName>
    <label>[Nation-Rank] Harp God</label>
    <description>Five strings run the length of the riser and only one of them is the bowstring. The other four are tuned. They answer when it is drawn, and what they are tuned to is not a note anyone has managed to write down — two people who tried agreed on the shape of it and on nothing else.\n\nIt is the only one of the seven that was never given to anybody. Every other file in the vault names a bearer. This one names the people who put it down again, and the list is longer than the guild is comfortable with.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Weapons/Harp_God</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(0.75,1.80)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <techLevel>Ultra</techLevel>
    <ignoreIllegalLabelCharacterConfigError>true</ignoreIllegalLabelCharacterConfigError>
    <uiIconScale>1.08</uiIconScale>
    <soundInteract>Bow_Large</soundInteract>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>16200</MarketValue>
      <MaxHitPoints>340</MaxHitPoints>
      <Mass>2.8</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.05</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>0.3</DeteriorationRate>
      <!-- The best accuracy profile in the line at every single band. A
           Nation weapon is allowed to have no bad range. -->
      <AccuracyTouch>0.88</AccuracyTouch>
      <AccuracyShort>0.98</AccuracyShort>
      <AccuracyMedium>0.96</AccuracyMedium>
      <AccuracyLong>0.88</AccuracyLong>
      <RangedWeapon_Cooldown>1.00</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
    </statBases>
    <weaponClasses><li>Ranged</li><li>RangedHeavy</li><li>LongShots</li><li>Ultratech</li></weaponClasses>
    <weaponTags><li>IsekaiDungeonArtifact</li></weaponTags>
    <tradeability>Sellable</tradeability>   <!-- gate rewards only: players may sell, traders never stock -->
    <thingCategories><li>WeaponsRanged</li></thingCategories>
    <!-- THE COST IS MELEE, and it is the only honest one available to a
         harp. Everything else here is a straight upgrade because that is
         what Nation rank is for, and because the last time this line got a
         heavy MoveSpeed penalty the verdict was that -0.55 is punishing on
         a weapon this hard to get. A -0.35 melee hit chance is felt
         exactly when the bow has already failed you and never before. -->
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <ShootingAccuracyPawn>0.35</ShootingAccuracyPawn>
      <AimingDelayFactor>-0.25</AimingDelayFactor>
      <MoveSpeed>0.20</MoveSpeed>
      <MeleeHitChance>-0.35</MeleeHitChance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <comps>
      <li><compClass>CompQuality</compClass></li>
      <li><compClass>IsekaiDungeons.CompArtifactQuality</compClass></li>
    </comps>
    <verbs>
      <li>
        <verbClass>Verb_Shoot</verbClass>
        <hasStandardCommand>true</hasStandardCommand>
        <defaultProjectile>IsekaiDungeons_Arrow_HarpGod</defaultProjectile>
        <warmupTime>1.10</warmupTime>
        <burstShotCount>3</burstShotCount>
        <ticksBetweenBurstShots>7</ticksBetweenBurstShots>
        <range>35.9</range>
        <soundCast>Bow_Large</soundCast>
      </li>
    </verbs>
    <tools>
      <li><label>frame</label><capacities><li>Blunt</li><li>Poke</li></capacities><power>18</power><cooldownTime>2.0</cooldownTime><armorPenetration>0.18</armorPenetration></li>
    </tools>
  </ThingDef>

  <!--
    ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    THE SHAFTS
    ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    All seven use damageDef Arrow rather than an elemental type. That is a
    deliberate restraint: Burn and Frostbite carry real side effects (fire
    spread, hypothermia, different armour interaction, different injury
    tables) that would make each bow behave in ways its stat block does
    not admit to. These are stat weapons, so the damage type stays honest.

    Speed climbs with rank. It is not cosmetic - a faster shaft spends
    less time in flight, so it is harder for a moving target to walk out
    of, which is a real advantage that costs no DPS on the info card.

    stoppingPower is set above a vanilla arrow's 1.5 on the heavy single
    shots, so Lavander Rose and Unicorn Star actually interrupt what they
    hit rather than just hurting it.
  -->

